<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="i-theming">Theming</h2>
  <p>Everything is a CSS custom property — override inline or in your own
     stylesheet, no rebuild. <code>--_</code>-prefixed properties are internal
     state tokens and not part of the API.</p>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Token</th><th>Affects</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-tabs-h</code></td><td>Bar height for text tabs (default 48px; icon tabs set 72px)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-tabs-transform</code></td><td>Label case — <code>uppercase</code> by default (M2); <code>none</code> for Google's web-app sentence case</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-accent</code></td><td>Selected label, indicator, focus ring</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-text-secondary</code></td><td>Inactive label</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-divider</code></td><td>Bar divider, pressed cell fill</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-hover</code></td><td>Inactive cell hover fill</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-disabled</code></td><td>Disabled label, muted indicator when the current tab is disabled</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% set themeExample %}
:root {
  --fl-tabs-transform: none;   /* sentence-case labels, Gmail-web style */
  --fl-accent: #188038;        /* indicator and selected label */
}
{% endset %}
  {{ snippet(themeExample) }}
  <p>M2 sets tab labels in all caps. Google's own web apps moved to sentence
     case, so the case is a token rather than a hard-coded rule — the padding,
     weight and 14px size stay put either way.</p>
</section>
{% endset %}

